## Objective
- Complete round-1 adversarial review of phase-098 (iteration helpers + `lru_cache` memoisation) and emit findings in the reviewer contract's exact format, ending with `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`.

## Important Details
- Repo/checkout: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`; phase `phase-098`; commit range `e39f70698f3aa698b50d01ac589fec39d1e5ea69..HEAD`.
- Contract: every finding cites `file:line` actually read; every `[BLOCKER]` MUST carry `VERIFIED:` (ran something, or traced exact path and quoted the line); otherwise downgrade to `[MAJOR]`. Do not report anything an existing test asserts is correct.
- Output format must be exactly `FINDINGS:` list with `BLOCKER|MAJOR|MINOR|STYLE`, then final line `REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS <count>` or `REVIEW VERDICT: CLEAN`; nothing after verdict.
- Phase adds helpers `chain`, `zip`, `enumerate`, `product`, `groupby`, `take`, `skip` and the `lru_cache(n) to f(...)` decorator (default 128), across tree-walker and bytecode VM; REPORT claims gates pass (2304 tests, fmt, clippy, `./rbops/verify.sh phase-098`).
- Candidate findings identified so far (severity assignment in progress):
  - BLOCKER: `give back skip(...)` / `return skip(...)` silently yields no value. `src/parser.rs:630`/`:639` gate on `is_expression_start()`, but `kind_starts_expression` (`src/parser.rs:1936-1953`) omits `TokenKind::Skip`; `skip(` arm exists only at `src/parser.rs:620-622` and primary. Result: `GiveBack(None)` plus separate `Expr(Call skip)` statement. Same gap breaks `might fail skip(...)` (`src/parser.rs:2061`). Fix: treat `skip(` as expression start for these gates.
  - BLOCKER/MAJOR: unbounded host recursion in bytecode cache hits. `src/bytecode/vm.rs:3176-3190` hit path calls `advance_map(self.frames.len()-1, value)`; `advance_map` (`:3130`) calls `call_function` (`:3144`); N consecutive cache hits recurse N frames, `call_depth` unchecked, no step/iteration charge. Repro: pre-call decorated f for N distinct args (capacity ≥ N), then `map` over N elements → all hits → stack overflow. `start_map` doc (`:3099`) explicitly warns per-element host recursion is avoided for misses.
  - MAJOR: cache identity is only `function.name`; object method sharing a name with a decorated function reads/writes that function's cache. Tree-walker: `src/interpreter.rs:2879` method call → `call_user_function`; lookup `:3002-3008`, insert `:3087-3090` keyed `function.name`. Object method `to can f(n)` and top-level `lru_cache(...) to f(n)` collide: `f(1)` then `Thing.f(1)` answers the cached function result, or method call poisons `f`'s cache. Bytecode equivalent `src/bytecode/vm.rs:3176-3179`, `:3240-3241`. REPORT's known-gap ("two same-named declarations in different scopes") does not cleanly cover a method namespace collision.
  - MINOR: SURVEY re-anchored citations point at wrong lines. `SURVEY.md:9` cites `src/stdlib.rs:1200` for `BUILTIN_NAMES` (actual start `:1190`); `SURVEY.md:10` cites `"input"` at `:1292` (actual `:1282`); also `:1417` should be `:1407` (`to_text`), `:1514` should be `:1504` (`json_stringify`), `:563` should be `:526/:527` (`expect`/`assert`). `tests/stdlib_gap_survey_test.rs` only checks the cited line exists, so this passes.
  - MINOR: `docs/GRAMMAR.md` not updated for new syntax. `:278` `skip_statement = 'skip'` and `:294` `function_decl = 'to' ...` cannot derive `skip(xs, n)` as an expression or `lru_cache(n) to f(...)`.
  - Possible MINOR: `lru_cache(-1)` errors "must be a number, as in lru_cache(128)" because `-` tokenizes separately, not the "at least 1" capacity message.

